1
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:07,480
It's time for the memory sketch!

2
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:10,040
Please prepare paper and
something to write with.

3
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:11,680
Here's the question.

4
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:14,940
Our familiar friend, Ryo-san,
otherwise known as Kankichi Ryotsu,

5
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:18,200
please draw without looking at anything,
using only your memory.

6
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:22,420
We think we see someone all the time,
but human memory is unreliable.

7
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:26,660
What hairstyle does Ryo-san have,
and what do his eyebrows look like?

8
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,480
Can you draw him properly?

9
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:31,140
Are you ready?

10
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:33,460
Ready, set, start!

11
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:38,540
When you watch TV,

12
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:41,140
turn on the room lights and watch from a distance,
will you?

13
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:54,300
Anyone with no money, come to me.

14
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:59,060
I've got none either, but don't worry.

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,340
Look at the blue sky and the white clouds.

16
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:12,960
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

17
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:29,940
Anyone without a job, come to me.

18
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:34,560
I don't have one either, but don't worry.

19
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:42,140
Look at the blazing steel fleet.

20
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:48,300
Somehow, it'll all work out eventually.

21
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:53,580
You get it, right? Right, right.

22
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:57,480
Once you understand,
keep quiet and follow me.

23
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,900
Mr. Tsurupikarion

24
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:24,380
It's fully autumn now, isn't it?

25
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:29,800
On a nice day like this,
patrolling outside is the best.

26
00:02:30,220 --> 00:02:31,200
Hey, senpai.

27
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:33,700
Senpai.

28
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:38,640
Look away for just a moment
and this is what happens.

29
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:41,800
Like I'm going to work
on a nice day like this!

30
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,880
On days like this,
the best thing is to take a leisurely nap.

31
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:00,880
Why, why won't it sell?

32
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:04,740
Our company's hair removal cream
is a wonderful product, though.

33
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:08,880
If they'd just try it a little,
they'd surely see how good it is.

34
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:12,420
Maybe I'm just not cut out to be a salesman.

35
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:17,260
That's...

36
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:19,800
What a torture.

37
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:23,640
I've never seen hair that thick and strong.

38
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:27,460
Our product might lose to that.

39
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:29,900
No...

40
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:35,020
If even the salesman doesn't believe in his own product,
what's the point?

41
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:38,520
Now it's a showdown.

42
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:42,380
Will this man's torture win,
or our hair removal cream?

43
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:46,060
Well, then?

44
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:50,840
Yes! Our hair removal cream wins!

45
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:53,240
Just as I thought, our product is superior!

46
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:56,940
That one looks five times
tougher than arm hair.

47
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:59,880
Honestly, our product might lose after all.

48
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,920
No, our product is the best in the world!

49
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:05,660
There's no way it could lose
to some torture like that.

50
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:07,740
Showdown!

51
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:10,260
Well?

52
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:14,400
Yay, two straight wins!

53
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:17,780
T-this is...

54
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:20,680
a will that rejects
every hair-removal cream,

55
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:23,340
a razor that shows a strong will.

56
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:26,160
This is a formidable foe.

57
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:31,320
The greatest enemy has
appeared right before my eyes.

58
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:34,000
No, I mustn't back down here.

59
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,900
If I don't get past this match,

60
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:39,460
our product isn't truly
the world's number one yet.

61
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:46,620
Well?

62
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:56,100
This is clearly not going to be easy, is it?

63
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,680
Yes! Ten straight wins!

64
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:07,440
Our company's product
has won a complete victory!

65
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:11,040
Our hair-removal cream really
is the best in the world!

66
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:14,100
But the opponent was truly formidable.

67
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:16,960
I ended up using the whole bottle.

68
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:21,500
I was so absorbed earlier
that I didn't notice,

69
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:24,500
but isn't this man
possibly a police officer?

70
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:29,840
Maybe I've done something terrible.

71
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:37,720
There's no room left to write anything

72
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:41,780
Isn't there somewhere else we can doodle?

73
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:42,380
Hey, look.

74
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:45,580
There's a bald guy sleeping.

75
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:46,640
Isn't that Ryo-san?

76
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:49,820
No, Ryo-san isn't this bald.

77
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:52,440
I think he kind of looks like him, though.

78
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,280
His head looks kind of lonely, doesn't it?

79
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:56,220
Let's draw some hair on his head.

80
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:58,380
How's that?

81
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,800
Nice, let's draw a beard too.

82
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:05,000
How's that?

83
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:10,460
That's funny, but with that beard,

84
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:15,500
this hairstyle suits you better.

85
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:17,020
How's that?

86
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:19,060
Really.

87
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:22,340
What a great wig!

88
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:23,400
Looks like a bear.

89
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:24,480
Yeah.

90
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,580
Then let's make him a bear.

91
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:30,900
Painting it all is such a hassle.

92
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:32,940
Then let's make him a panda.

93
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:34,380
That's cuter, isn't it?

94
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,080
Done.

95
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:41,040
Not very cute, is it?

96
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:41,740
Yeah.

97
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:44,420
He looks like a panda-faced monster.

98
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:46,080
Whoa!

99
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,502
I slept well.

100
00:06:50,552 --> 00:06:53,864
Somehow,
it feels like things were noisy around me.

101
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:55,960
Guess I'll head home soon.

102
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:14,580
I kinda feel like everyone's staring at me.

103
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:15,280
Kenjara!

104
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:16,580
What?

105
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:18,740
It's your damn fault!

106
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:20,120
What? You're the one who's to blame!

107
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:21,180
Hey!

108
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:25,300
Hey, stop it!

109
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:26,640
Shut up!

110
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,060
Are you okay?

111
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:31,840
I'm fine.

112
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:34,700
Sorry, which one of you is it?

113
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:37,480
I'm asking what caused the fight!

114
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:39,720
You?

115
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:41,980
You?

116
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:46,440
We weren't fighting or anything.

117
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:47,380
Hey, I'm talking to you.

118
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:50,660
Is that true?

119
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:51,940
It's true.

120
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:53,940
We were just goofing around a little.

121
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:55,480
Better be true.

122
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:57,200
It's true.

123
00:07:57,710 --> 00:08:00,040
Don't you two ever fight again, got it?

124
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,100
Yes sir.

125
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:06,360
Who was that man, anyway?

126
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,380
No idea.

127
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:11,140
I just had a feeling that if we defied him,
something awful would happen.

128
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:12,620
Definitely.

129
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:15,420
Stopping a fight with just one glare.

130
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:18,820
Guess I'm developing some
real presence as a man too.

131
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:24,640
I'm back.

132
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:28,120
Is no one here?

133
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:30,580
Geez, what a pain.

134
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:31,880
Right.

135
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:36,820
Fitting for a man of my refinement,
I'll stand guard out front, nice and cool.

136
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:48,100
It's full-on autumn now, so cool. It's the
perfect season for a cool guy like Ryotsu.

137
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:50,420
And you tsumo'd it in one shot for a baiman!

138
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:55,820
Bro, your luck's been on fire lately.
I'm going all in on you for the next G1 too.

139
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:57,580
Don't go scamming me.

140
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:00,280
Ugh.

141
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,020
Hot!

142
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:01,400
Hot!

143
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:01,960
Hot!

144
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:02,800
Hot!

145
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:04,980
Hot!

146
00:09:04,980 --> 00:09:05,320
Hot!

147
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,040
Hot!

148
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:06,380
Hot!

149
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:06,540
Hot!

150
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:06,700
Hot!

151
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:08,960
Hot!

152
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:11,080
How was it, Divisional Chief?

153
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:13,480
How do you find the situation in
our Katsushika precinct jurisdiction?

154
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:17,160
Very well managed. Impressive.

155
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:17,980
Thank you.

156
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:23,300
There's a police box over there.

157
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:26,540
Damn, that's the one I
didn't want you to see!

158
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:28,100
Stop the car.

159
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:28,880
Yes.

160
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:33,740
Lunch is ready for you at the station,
Chief, so

161
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,700
This won't take long.

162
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:41,440
Please, let Ryotsu not be here.

163
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:43,820
Is anyone there?

164
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:47,420
Good, Ryotsu doesn't seem to be here.

165
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:50,540
Coming, coming!

166
00:09:50,540 --> 00:09:52,300
It's Ryotsu!

167
00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:56,260
Looks like a toilet, doesn't it?

168
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:59,120
Chief.

169
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,840
Divisional Chief, Chief!

170
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,920
Thank you for your inspection, sir.

171
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:07,880
Ryotsu, is it?

172
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:12,820
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu,
stationed at the Kameari Park police box.

173
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:16,080
Y-you always make that face?

174
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:19,500
Of course, sir!
The police box is the face of the police.

175
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:25,420
As long as I'm at this police box, the ten million
citizens of Tokyo can rest easy, Divisional Chief.

176
00:10:25,420 --> 00:10:29,860
I see. Tomita,
you don't seem to be feeling well.

177
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:33,640
Let's call it a day today.
That would be best, I think.

178
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:39,120
Take care.

179
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:46,200
The Divisional Chief was also intimidated by my presence,
it seems.

180
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:54,960
I'm back.

181
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:55,680
I'm home.

182
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:56,920
Hey, you're late.

183
00:10:56,920 --> 00:11:00,100
You're the senior officer, right?

184
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:02,380
Who else would it be?

185
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:08,920
My face has gained quite a bit of dignity,
hasn't it?

186
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:13,600
A man over thirty has to win with his face,
you know.

187
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:17,140
How about this face?
Doesn't it look like Ken Takakura?

188
00:11:17,140 --> 00:11:18,780
I wonder.

189
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:22,300
Hey, Ryo-chan,
is he seriously wearing that makeup?

190
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:23,560
I don't know.

191
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:27,460
Sometimes the senior officer comes
up with the most outrageous ideas.

192
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:28,380
That's right.

193
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:36,620
Well, let's take a photo together to
commemorate Ryo-chan becoming cool.

194
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:37,960
Sounds good.

195
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:39,520
Kei-chan, please.

196
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:40,380
Yes.

197
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,240
Okay, here we go.

198
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:48,660
Look, it's coming out.

199
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:52,780
It must have come out cool.
Let's see, let's see.

200
00:11:56,820 --> 00:11:59,160
What's this? Who's this goofy-faced guy?

201
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:04,820
Is that me?

202
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:06,520
Yes.

203
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:09,340
W-what the hell is this!

204
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,980
So you really didn't notice

205
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:14,540
Did you think something was off?

206
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,463
T-this is...

207
00:12:16,513 --> 00:12:18,820
Not cool at all!

208
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:38,640
Phew, so it was just Comet Magic after all

209
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:41,800
When did you end up looking like that?

210
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:44,420
I don't know. I have no memory of it at all.

211
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:48,240
When I took off the makeup,
I ended up with an alien's face.

212
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:51,060
It looks unnatural without eyebrows.

213
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:52,840
I see.

214
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:54,820
I'll draw eyebrows on
you with an eyebrow pencil.

215
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:57,600
Please do. Like this, I look creepy.

216
00:12:58,660 --> 00:13:01,340
By the way, what kind of
eyebrows did Ryo-chan have again?

217
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:04,700
I rarely look at my own face, so.

218
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:08,520
Was it like this?

219
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:11,780
It feels like the vibe is a bit off.

220
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:14,540
Let me borrow that for a moment.

221
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:15,020
Here you go.

222
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:18,840
I'm pretty sure his eyebrows were thicker.

223
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,200
Like this, then.

224
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:22,400
They look like a snowman's eyebrows.

225
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,240
Something's off.

226
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:27,480
So they were connected.

227
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:30,940
Right, if I draw them connected,
that should work, shouldn't it?

228
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:34,480
So, like this, like this

229
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,920
It's a bit too plain, isn't it?

230
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:40,640
Then how about drawing a tulip here?

231
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:43,500
Haha, it suits him!

232
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:47,020
If we're going to do it,
draw a sun above that too.

233
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:51,020
Then I'll draw a cute little house.

234
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:55,380
Then I'll add some flowers around the house.

235
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:56,560
How cute!

236
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:59,160
That's enough!
Stop playing around on people's foreheads!

237
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,080
Sorry, I just couldn't help it.

238
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:03,260
I'll draw it myself!

239
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:06,380
When he gets angry with that face,
he's several times scarier.

240
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,800
Leave it to me, you two.

241
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,240
Are you all right?

242
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:14,500
It's my own face,
one I've lived with for over 30 years.

243
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:15,620
It'll be fine.

244
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:17,060
How about this? This is it, right?

245
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:18,860
That's a bit off.

246
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:22,240
That makes him look like
the hero of a superhero manga.

247
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,320
Really?

248
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:26,760
His eyebrows were connected, you know.

249
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:27,920
Like this.

250
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:29,980
That's right.

251
00:14:29,980 --> 00:14:33,800
How about drawing
eyeliner while we're at it?

252
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:38,780
With this, you look like a kabuki actor!

253
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:42,920
Since your head's looking lonely up top,
let us draw some flowers.

254
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,580
A flower garden, right here.

255
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:47,120
That's why you're not an illustration board.

256
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,920
Don't draw whatever you want!

257
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,620
Drawing with Reiko's Mekarape, you idiots.

258
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:53,380
It won't come off at all!

259
00:14:53,380 --> 00:14:55,100
I'll write your name on the back.

260
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:56,560
In a cute pink.

261
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,700
Then we'd better draw your address too.

262
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,540
That's enough!

263
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:07,160
Who on earth writes their address
and name on a high schooler?

264
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:13,700
I'm back from the station.

265
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:15,220
Goburo.

266
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:48,580
I'm sure I left it in my pocket.

267
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:49,620
It's not there?

268
00:15:49,900 --> 00:15:52,780
I don't remember taking it out,
so it should be somewhere in there.

269
00:15:57,660 --> 00:15:58,640
My notebook!

270
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:04,660
Kana, kana...

271
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:09,160
Alright, looks like it's fine.

272
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:10,100
Found it!

273
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:30,080
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

274
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:32,207
If I think about it,
as long as it's a photo,

275
00:16:32,257 --> 00:16:35,040
it doesn't have to be a
photo for the police ID, right?

276
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:36,440
I see.

277
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:40,380
I'm sure there's a photo we all
took together in summer somewhere.

278
00:16:40,780 --> 00:16:41,420
Where is it?

279
00:16:42,020 --> 00:16:43,360
I think it's on top of the locker.

280
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:46,640
That one?

281
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:49,640
Alright, let's go, just a sec.

282
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:52,580
No way!

283
00:16:53,160 --> 00:17:01,900
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

284
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:11,660
Only the part where Senpai
is in came out nicely

285
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:13,100
This one too.

286
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:15,040
This one too.

287
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:16,760
This one too.

288
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:17,900
Terrible.

289
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:21,380
It was Ryo-san who told
us to get the stove going.

290
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:24,820
Don't go pulling out the stove
when it's not even that cold.

291
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:26,300
Just put it back outside already.

292
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:27,500
Fine, fine.

293
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:28,320
Ugh.

294
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:33,800
There's no point keeping it here, you know.

295
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:35,200
What are you trying to say?

296
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:37,480
It's nothing.

297
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:39,180
But this is a real problem.

298
00:17:39,180 --> 00:17:42,560
Who else might have a photo of Senpai?

299
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:45,140
Maria-san.

300
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,180
Lord Ryo.

301
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:49,480
Poor Lord Ryo.

302
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:51,280
Look what's happened to him.

303
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:54,420
If you think so,
hurry up and do something about it.

304
00:17:54,980 --> 00:17:57,120
I asked Maria-chan on the phone.

305
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:02,020
Yes! I always carry Ryo-sama's
photos close to my heart!

306
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:02,960
Endory?

307
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:04,520
What the heck is this?!

308
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:07,500
This is the photo from the costume contest!

309
00:18:07,550 --> 00:18:09,660
You can't tell what his real
face looks like from this, right?

310
00:18:10,180 --> 00:18:12,080
But he was so cute!

311
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:15,320
Don't you have any other photos?
Ones where you can actually see his face...

312
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:16,929
Don't worry!

313
00:18:16,979 --> 00:18:19,800
Ryo-sama's photos are all neatly organized

314
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:22,500
in a single album!

315
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:26,500
It's called
"Ryo-sama and Maria's Album of Love!"

316
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:30,720
Never mind that,
where is this album of yours?

317
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:33,640
Yes, I brought it with me, of course.

318
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:35,080
It's right here on the desk.

319
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:38,540
Fine.

320
00:18:38,540 --> 00:18:41,400
Our album of love, Ryo-sama and mine,

321
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:43,660
is completely ruined, isn't it?

322
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,780
Poor Maria-chan.

323
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:49,000
Why did you leave the
stove in a place like that?

324
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,780
Ryo-san said to leave it outside.

325
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:52,740
Shut up!

326
00:18:56,580 --> 00:18:59,740
When it comes down to it, it's really
hard to remember a person's face, isn't it?

327
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:02,720
Even though we should
see him almost every day.

328
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:07,260
I feel like Ryo-sama's eyebrows
were really distinctive, though.

329
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:10,120
I think they were thick and connected,

330
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,920
I feel like we need
some flowers around here.

331
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:15,120
And draw a house over here.

332
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:16,540
Stop it already!

333
00:19:16,540 --> 00:19:18,680
I'm sorry, Ryo-sama.

334
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:23,040
Ryo-chan's head is just the kind of shape that makes you want to doodle on it,
isn't it?

335
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:25,700
Anyway,
we can't get any work done like this.

336
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:28,300
Let's get a wig and some false eyelashes.

337
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:30,820
Something looks unnatural.

338
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:33,080
He doesn't look like Ryo-sama at all.

339
00:19:33,620 --> 00:19:35,320
He looks like Honda-san.

340
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:38,040
Then let's try it in
Terai-san's style this time.

341
00:19:38,580 --> 00:19:39,700
This is weird too.

342
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:43,320
I feel like I've turned
into a petty bourgeois.

343
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:45,560
I tried it in Sakonji-san's style.

344
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:46,960
That's not it.

345
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:50,720
- Let's do it in Reiko's style!
- Stop it!

346
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:53,500
- Komachi-chan style!
- Nakagawa-kun style!

347
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:56,520
None of them are quite right. Yeah.

348
00:19:57,240 --> 00:20:00,360
- How about this one?
- It's in Chief Ohara's style.

349
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:04,180
This is the best one so far. Yes, I agree.

350
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,480
It gives off a bad vibe.

351
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:10,420
Well, he's really gone, isn't he.

352
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:14,720
Oh no, what have we done.

353
00:20:14,770 --> 00:20:16,720
We got carried away.

354
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,360
Let's honestly report it to the police.

355
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:24,900
Yes, what is it?

356
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:28,680
I feel like we've met somewhere before...

357
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:29,360
Me?

358
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:29,780
Yeah.

359
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:31,840
I don't remember you.

360
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:33,840
No, somewhere recently...

361
00:20:35,660 --> 00:20:36,640
W-what?

362
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:38,180
Maybe it's the hairstyle?

363
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:41,000
What do you think you're doing?

364
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
S-sorry, sorry!

365
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,840
I-I knew it...

366
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:46,440
S-s-sorry!

367
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,780
Yes, see you later!

368
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:49,440
Oi, wait!

369
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:51,380
Wait!

370
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:54,420
Get back here!

371
00:20:56,860 --> 00:20:58,100
Get back here!

372
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:02,500
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

373
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,880
What exactly are you sorry for?

374
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:06,720
I was actually planning to apologize,
I swear!

375
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:08,620
So what is this all about?

376
00:21:09,020 --> 00:21:11,880
I'll come clean honestly,
so please forgive us.

377
00:21:13,020 --> 00:21:14,960
What? A hair remover?

378
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:17,360
Yes, that explains it.

379
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:20,240
That's what you get for slacking
off and napping on the job.

380
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,340
Shut up.

381
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:24,940
Isn't there some way to fix this?

382
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:25,700
Yes.

383
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:29,040
I panicked earlier and ran away, but

384
00:21:29,740 --> 00:21:31,940
actually, we have something for this.

385
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:35,040
Our product is so powerful that

386
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:37,280
in case someone accidentally
removes too much hair,

387
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:40,380
we also sell a powerful
hair-growth tonic as a set.

388
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:41,400
I see.

389
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:44,560
If you apply this medicine
to restore the original shape,

390
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:47,020
it'll be back to normal in no time.

391
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:52,440
You must be struggling because you can't
tell what its original shape was, right?

392
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,540
Is that so?

393
00:21:55,540 --> 00:21:58,240
Hey, what are you doing, Ryotsu?

394
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,440
Chief.

395
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:01,000
Chief.

396
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:04,440
Chief, can you recognize my face?

397
00:22:05,020 --> 00:22:08,100
Of course I can. How many years do
you think we've known each other?

398
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:13,060
Anyway, that face of yours is embarrassing,
so do something about it.

399
00:22:13,060 --> 00:22:16,060
I want to do something about it too.

400
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:18,700
But I can't remember my original face.

401
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:19,340
What?

402
00:22:20,260 --> 00:22:23,480
I accidentally depilated
myself with hair-removal cream.

403
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:26,400
So I'm trying to restore it to how it was.

404
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:28,440
But I've lost track of what
my original face looked like.

405
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:30,500
Is that all it is?

406
00:22:30,940 --> 00:22:32,260
If it's Ryotsu's face,

407
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:37,280
The eyebrows go like this,

408
00:22:39,080 --> 00:22:40,380
the hair goes like this.

409
00:22:40,940 --> 00:22:43,400
And a warrior's mustache, too.

410
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:45,520
How's that?

411
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:50,160
It's Lord Ryo, indeed.

412
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:52,100
Yes, yes, that's the face!

413
00:22:52,820 --> 00:22:54,460
Somehow, that's a relief.

414
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:55,060
Yeah.

415
00:22:55,780 --> 00:22:57,300
That's my face.

416
00:22:57,980 --> 00:23:01,940
Honestly, what are you fussing
over with something this trivial?

417
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:04,420
So we can paint it exactly like this,
correct?

418
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:05,780
Go ahead.

419
00:23:11,240 --> 00:23:13,160
The eyebrows are done. Next is

420
00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:15,220
It's already growing back!

421
00:23:16,060 --> 00:23:18,960
This is a newly developed,
super-strong type.

422
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:22,340
After all, our company's products
are the best in the world.

423
00:23:22,340 --> 00:23:25,400
But isn't it growing a little too fast?

424
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:27,620
Yeah, it's way too fast.

425
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:30,760
What are you talking about?
You'd better hurry and make me normal again!

426
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:33,980
Wh-wh-what?

427
00:23:37,920 --> 00:23:39,260
Too strong!

428
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:42,560
Sorry.

429
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:44,840
After all, our company's products are

430
00:23:46,060 --> 00:23:47,040
number one, after all!

431
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:56,720
Look, Ryo-san!

432
00:23:57,240 --> 00:23:59,480
It's not my fault!

433
00:24:00,060 --> 00:24:01,540
Eyebrows, boing!

434
00:24:16,060 --> 00:24:20,440
Like the morning calling out,
an afternoon after the rain

435
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:27,160
walking while looking back,
led by the hand by Gacha

436
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:34,160
that strange feeling I had back then

437
00:24:35,180 --> 00:24:39,540
so, the tiles of the arcade street

438
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:45,320
I walked only on the black ones

439
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:53,620
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

440
00:24:54,540 --> 00:25:01,000
even the politicians with their self-important
faces and the aunties with blue eyeshadow

441
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:06,580
Go on, turn that corner

442
00:25:07,820 --> 00:25:11,740
you can meet everyone, everyone

443
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:16,500
That's Kameary over there

444
00:25:17,500 --> 00:25:19,840
Well, surely it's Kameary

445
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:24,960
Everybody, come on over to our town!

446
00:25:26,040 --> 00:25:26,520
Thank you.

447
00:25:29,920 --> 00:25:31,260
Hey, hey, you're being too cute about it.

448
00:25:31,260 --> 00:25:35,320
Why is your room so cluttered with stuff?

449
00:25:36,580 --> 00:25:38,520
You can't turn down salespeople,
so you end up buying things?

450
00:25:38,580 --> 00:25:39,660
Are you an idiot?

451
00:25:39,660 --> 00:25:40,860
You know, things like that -

452
00:25:40,860 --> 00:25:43,500
you just refuse them with one word:
"No thanks."

453
00:25:43,500 --> 00:25:44,400
Next time:

454
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:46,520
Blow away those shady salesmen!

455
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:47,800
See you then.

